MVP architecture
Core pieces
1. SDK

Used in the customer app/backend to define agents and tools.

2. Control plane API

Creates sessions, stores metadata, issues tokens, receives events.

3. Realtime gateway

Handles WebSocket or SSE connections for chat streams.

4. Agent runtime service

Runs the model loop:

append message
call model
stream tokens
detect tool calls
invoke tool
feed result back to model
continue until final answer
5. Session store

Stores:

threads
messages
tool calls
run metadata
model/provider config
6. Tool execution adapter

For MVP, probably customer-hosted HTTPS tools or in-process tools from their backend SDK.

